# Wilfred BSD Configuration Example

This is a sample configuration for BSD systems (FreeBSD, OpenBSD, NetBSD, DragonFly).
Copy to `~/.config/wilfred/wilfred.yml` and adjust as needed.

```yaml
# Wilfred configuration for BSD systems
# Generated: {{date}}
# See docs/configuration.md for full schema

# =============================================================================
# Index roots - directories to index
# =============================================================================
index:
  roots:
    - "~/Documents"
    - "~/Downloads"
    - "~/Projects"
    - "~/Code"
    - "/usr/local/share/applications"
    - "/usr/share/applications"
    - "/opt"
  # Exclude patterns (glob)
  excludes:
    - "*/.git/*"
    - "*/node_modules/*"
    - "*/__pycache__/*"
    - "*/target/*"
    - "*/build/*"
    - "*.tmp"
    - "*.swp"
    - "*.bak"
  # Follow symlinks
  follow_symlinks: false
  # Rescan interval (0 = disabled, use watcher only)
  rescan_interval_hours: 24

# =============================================================================
# Watcher - filesystem monitoring
# =============================================================================
watcher:
  # Debounce milliseconds (BSD kqueue is event-driven, low debounce OK)
  debounce_ms: 50
  # Enable recursive watching (kqueue watches directories individually)
  recursive: true

# =============================================================================
# Search ranking weights
# =============================================================================
ranking:
  # Base weights (sum should be ~100 for normalized scores)
  name_match: 40        # Exact/substring name match
  path_match: 15        # Path component match
  acronym: 25           # Acronym/initialism match (e.g. "vsc" -> "Visual Studio Code")
  fuzzy: 15             # Fuzzy/Damerau match
  recency: 5            # Recently accessed files
  frequency: 3          # Frequently accessed files
  pinned: 50            # Pinned favorites (large boost)
  # Context signals
  recent_folders: 8     # Files in recently visited folders
  file_type_affinity: 6 # Preferred file types per query context
  time_of_day: 4        # Time-based usage patterns
  session_queries: 3    # Queries in current session

# =============================================================================
# Global hotkey
# =============================================================================
hotkey:
  key: "w"
  modifiers: ["ctrl", "alt"]
  # macOS: use "cmd" instead of "ctrl"
  # use_command_on_macos: true

# =============================================================================
# UI overlay appearance
# =============================================================================
ui:
  # Transparent glass panel (requires compositor)
  transparent: true
  # Backdrop blur (requires compositor + GPU)
  blur: true
  # Glass opacity (0.0 - 1.0)
  opacity: 0.85
  # Accent color (hex or named: indigo, blue, green, teal, pink, orange, red, purple, violet)
  accent: "indigo"
  # Base font size (10-24)
  font_size: 14
  # Max results to show
  max_results: 40
  # Animation duration (ms)
  animation_ms: 170

# =============================================================================
# File actions
# =============================================================================
actions:
  # Per-application extra actions
  app_actions:
    "code":
      - "Open in VS Code"
      - "Open folder in VS Code"
    "firefox":
      - "Open in Firefox"
    "vim":
      - "Edit with Vim"
    "emacs":
      - "Edit with Emacs"
  # Named workflows (chained actions)
  workflows:
    "review":
      - "open"
      - "copy_path"
    "edit_compile":
      - "open_editor"
      - "open_terminal"
    "backup":
      - "copy_path"
      - "compress_zip"

# =============================================================================
# Quicklinks (parameterized)
# =============================================================================
quicklinks:
  "gh":
    url: "https://github.com/{1}"
    desc: "Open GitHub repo"
  "man":
    url: "https://man.openbsd.org/{1}"
    desc: "OpenBSD man page"
  "pkg":
    url: "https://www.freebsd.org/cgi/ports.cgi?query={1}&stype=all"
    desc: "FreeBSD port search"
  "src":
    url: "https://src.freebsd.org/search/?q={1}"
    desc: "FreeBSD source search"

# =============================================================================
# Macros (bang searches)
# =============================================================================
macros:
  "!man": "man {query}"
  "!pkg": "pkg search {query}"
  "!bsd": "https://www.freebsd.org/search/?q={query}"
  "!obsd": "https://man.openbsd.org/{query}"
  "!nbsd": "https://man.netbsd.org/{query}"
  "!dfly": "https://man.dragonflybsd.org/{query}"

# =============================================================================
# Package managers
# =============================================================================
packages:
  # Explicitly enabled managers (empty = auto-detect)
  managers:
    - "pkg"
    - "pkgin"
    - "pkg_add"
    - "flatpak"
    - "brew"
  # Per-manager options
  options:
    pkg:
      timeout_ms: 15000
    pkgin:
      timeout_ms: 15000
    pkg_add:
      timeout_ms: 15000

# =============================================================================
# System toggles (BSD-specific)
# =============================================================================
toggles:
  # WiFi - requires wpa_supplicant/ifconfig
  wifi:
    enabled: true
    interface: "wlan0"  # FreeBSD/DragonFly
    # OpenBSD: "iwn0", "urtwn0", etc.
    # NetBSD: "wlan0", "ural0", etc.
  # Bluetooth - not yet implemented on BSD
  bluetooth:
    enabled: false
  # Volume - OSS mixer (FreeBSD/DragonFly), sndio (OpenBSD), sysctl (NetBSD)
  volume:
    enabled: true
    step: 5
  # Brightness - backlight/intel_backlight/acpi_video
  brightness:
    enabled: true
    step: 10

# =============================================================================
# Power actions
# =============================================================================
power:
  # Sleep command per OS
  sleep_cmd:
    freebsd: "acpiconf -s 3"
    dragonfly: "acpiconf -s 3"
    openbsd: "zzz"
    netbsd: "sysctl -w hw.acpi.sleep.state=3"
  # Shutdown
  shutdown_cmd: "shutdown -p now"
  # Restart
  restart_cmd: "shutdown -r now"
  # Logout - try desktop session managers
  logout_cmd: "gnome-session-quit --logout --no-prompt || xfce4-session-logout --logout || mate-session-save --logout || qdbus org.kde.ksmserver /KSMServer logout 0 0 0"

# =============================================================================
# Editor/Terminal preferences
# =============================================================================
editor:
  # Preferred editors (first available wins)
  preferences:
    - "code"
    - "codium"
    - "vim"
    - "nvim"
    - "emacs"
    - "mg"
    - "ee"

terminal:
  preferences:
    - "foot"
    - "alacritty"
    - "kitty"
    - "wezterm"
    - "gnome-terminal"
    - "konsole"
    - "xfce4-terminal"
    - "xterm"

# =============================================================================
# History
# =============================================================================
history:
  enabled: true
  max_entries: 1000
  # Persist across sessions
  persist: true

# =============================================================================
# Clipboard
# =============================================================================
clips:
  max_entries: 500
  persist: true
  # Types to track
  types: ["text", "url", "email", "path", "code", "ip", "image"]

# =============================================================================
# Snippets
# =============================================================================
snippets:
  auto_paste: true
  # Global abbreviations (expand anywhere)
  global_abbreviations: false

# =============================================================================
# Backup/Sync
# =============================================================================
sync:
  # Local backup directory
  backup_dir: "~/Backups/Wilfred"
  # Remote sync (optional)
  remote:
    enabled: false
    # url: "sftp://user@host/path"
    # or: "rclone:remote:path"

# =============================================================================
# Logging
# =============================================================================
logging:
  level: "info"  # debug, info, warn, error
  # File logging
  file:
    enabled: true
    path: "~/.local/share/wilfred/logs/wilfred.log"
    max_size_mb: 10
    max_files: 5
  # Console logging (daemon mode)
  console: false

# =============================================================================
# Advanced
# =============================================================================
advanced:
  # IPC socket path (empty = default)
  ipc_socket: ""
  # Query timeout (ms)
  query_timeout_ms: 5000
  # Plugin timeout (ms)
  plugin_timeout_ms: 3000
  # Max concurrent searches
  max_concurrent_searches: 4
```

## BSD-Specific Notes

### FreeBSD
- WiFi interface typically `wlan0`, `wlan1`, etc.
- Volume via OSS `mixer`
- Sleep via `acpiconf -s 3`
- Package manager: `pkg`
- Ports: `/usr/ports`, packages in `/usr/local`

### OpenBSD
- WiFi interface varies: `iwn0`, `urtwn0`, `athn0`, etc.
- Volume via `sndio`/`mixerctl`
- Sleep via `zzz`
- Package manager: `pkg_add`/`pkg_info`
- No `sudo` by default; use `doas` or run as root
- `pledge`/`unveil` restrictions apply

### NetBSD
- WiFi interface: `wlan0`, `ural0`, `athn0`, etc.
- Volume via `sysctl hw.snd.vpc_*`
- Sleep via `sysctl -w hw.acpi.sleep.state=3`
- Package manager: `pkgin`
- `getvfsstat` instead of `getmntinfo`

### DragonFly BSD
- Similar to FreeBSD
- WiFi: `wlan0`
- Volume: OSS `mixer`
- Sleep: `acpiconf -s 3`
- Package manager: `pkg`
- HAMMER2 filesystem support

## File Manager Integration

The `open_parent` action (Ctrl+Enter on a file result) opens the containing
folder in your preferred file manager. Supported managers (auto-detected):

- Thunar (Xfce)
- Dolphin (KDE)
- Nautilus/Files (GNOME)
- Nemo (Cinnamon)
- PCManFM (LXDE)
- Caja (MATE)
- SpaceFM
- Worker
- Terminal: lf, ranger, nnn, vifm
- Krusader, Double Commander

If none detected, falls back to `xdg-open`.

## Building on BSD

```bash
# FreeBSD
pkg install cmake ninja pkgconf shells/bash git
./scripts/build-bsd.sh --release --tests

# OpenBSD
pkg_add cmake ninja pkgconf bash git
./scripts/build-bsd.sh --release --tests

# NetBSD
pkgin install cmake ninja pkgconf shells/bash git
./scripts/build-bsd.sh --release --tests

# DragonFly
pkg install cmake ninja pkgconf shells/bash git
./scripts/build-bsd.sh --release --tests
```

Optional GUI dependencies:
```bash
# FreeBSD
pkg install webkit2-gtk3 gtk3 gtk-layer-shell libX11

# OpenBSD
pkg_add webkit2-gtk3 gtk+3 gtk-layer-shell libX11

# NetBSD
pkgin install webkit2-gtk3 gtk3 gtk-layer-shell libX11

# DragonFly
pkg install webkit2-gtk3 gtk3 gtk-layer-shell libX11
```